  "supportClaimEffect": "none",
  "purpose": "Resolve the legacy XRECORD string-length ambiguity for locally generated ODA R13/R14 codepage-45 controls.",
  "specificationConflict": "ODA DWG specification v5.4.1 section 20.4.104 describes a one-byte length followed by a one-byte codepage for legacy strings. These observed ODA File Converter files encode the length as a little-endian two-byte short followed by a one-byte codepage; the 256 and 300-byte controls distinguish the layouts. This is producer-specific evidence, not a claim that the specification or other producers use this encoding.",
  "generation": "Create DXF locally with ezdxf, convert to AC1012 and AC1014 with ODA File Converter, inspect LibreDWG-discovered object frames and their class records, then reopen each DWG with ODA and inspect resulting DXF with ezdxf. All files and mutations stay in scratch storage.",
  "verification": [
    "Physical type, EED terminator, length, codepage, string bytes, following group-90, object boundary, ownership, reactor and extension handles, CRC and following frame are checked.",
    "Malformed 300-byte count is changed to 65535 with a repaired frame CRC; candidate adapter records an object parse failure and successfully retries the original source on the same adapter.",
    "Fast generated controls cover both revisions and five counts, preserve the following value and handles, and verify reset and retry under ASan."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only the tested ODA producer and ASCII page-45 payloads are evidenced; no AutoCAD/ObjectARX producer, native dictionary cloning behavior, whole-source guards or output qualification is established.",
    "The ODA reopen is the same producer family; LibreDWG supplies independent object discovery and the research script separately inspects physical bytes."
  ],
